@pyq U.P. R.O. / A.R.O. (Mains) 2016
Which of the following statements is correct about 'India's Trade Gross Domestic Product' ratio?
(a) India's Trade GDP ratio has been more than 50% since 2000
(b) India's Trade GDP ratio was minimum in 2007
(c) India's Trade GDP ratio was 46.02% in 2019
(d) India's Trade GDP ratio in 2019 was less than 2018 by nearly 3.4%
@ans (*)
@note World Bank data put India's trade-GDP ratio at about **27% in 2000**, above **50% only in 2008 and 2011-2013**, about **44% in 2018** and **39.4% in 2019**. None of the statements is exactly right, so the source marks it (*).
@end
