@section 17.3 | Balance of Trade and Payments

@q 12:18-22

@src1 12:4
@one U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 1994
Balance of Payment is defined as
@ans Complete record of all economic transactions between residents of a country and the rest of the world
@end

@q 12:23

@table
Account | Contents
**Balance of trade** | **Goods** (visible) exports − imports; India runs a large **deficit**
**Current account** | Goods + **services (invisibles)** + income + **transfers** (remittances)
**Current account deficit** | Payments for goods, services, income and transfers exceed receipts; it comes from **importing more**, not exporting more
**Capital account** | FDI, FPI, loans (ECB), NRI deposits, banking capital
Net exports | **Exports − imports**
@end

India's trade deficit peaked in **2012-13** and fell after 2013-14 as both **oil and non-oil** deficits shrank, so the Reason explains the Assertion.

@section 17.4 | What India Imports

@q 12:24-29

@src1 12:5
@one U.P. Lower Sub. (Spl.) (Pre) 2004; U.P.P.C.S. (Spl.) (Mains) 2004
What has been the most important item in the total imports of India in recent years?
@ans Petroleum & Edible Oil
@end

**Crude oil and petroleum products** are India's largest import (about Rs. 15.7 lakh crore in 2024-25), followed by **electronics, gold, capital goods** and edible oil. **Qatar** is the biggest **LNG** supplier. An import begins with an **indent** (order), and the **importer** arranges the **letter of credit** through his bank.

